UID:court-list-06@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261120
SUMMARY:Supreme Court: The petition of two transparency activists on Delhi'
 s revision\, W.P.(C) No. 1188 of 2026\, and an application they were told 
 to file on the Commission's letter about Form 6
DESCRIPTION:The petition of two transparency activists on Delhi's revision\
 , W.P.(C) No. 1188 of 2026\, and an application they were told to file on 
 the Commission's letter about Form 6. The petition is listed for admission
  as item 26 in the Chief Justice's court\, before the Chief Justice\, Just
 ice Joymalya Bagchi and Justice V. Mohana\, with an application for clarif
 ication or direction and an intervention application. A connected petition
 \, W.P.(C) No. 1339 of 2026\, is listed with it as item 26.1. The court si
 ts from 10:30 am. On 4 November the Court declined to pass urgent orders a
 nd asked the petitioners to file their application before this date. Court
 : Supreme Court. Source: Supreme Court of India\, daily cause list for 19 
 November 2026\, https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/cl/2026-11-19/M_J_1.pdf More:
  https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-61
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:court-list-11@offtheroll.in
DTSTAMP:20261106T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Supreme Court (listed tentatively): The petitions on the restrictio
 ns imposed during the protests against the Chief Election Commissioner in 
 October\, led by MA Baby v
DESCRIPTION:The petitions on the restrictions imposed during the protests a
 gainst the Chief Election Commissioner in October\, led by MA Baby v. Unio
 n of India\, with which the Court will hear the petition of two traders' a
 ssociations on their business losses and on Ramlila Maidan as a protest si
 te\, W.P.(C) No. 1395 of 2026. The petitions are tentatively listed for he
 aring. On 18 November the Court issued notice on the traders' petition to 
 the Cockroach Janta Party\, the Congress\, the Aam Aadmi Party and the All
  India Students' Association\, and said it would be heard with these petit
 ions. The court listed the matter for this date tentatively. Court: Suprem
 e Court. Source: LiveLaw\, https://www.livelaw.in/top-stories/supreme-cour
 t-issues-notice-to-cjp-congress-aap-aisa-on-delhi-traders-plea-against-pro
 tests-558913 More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-court-88
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
